 "content_notes": "Closed: Robert Durst was convicted of the first-degree murder of Susan Berman on 17 September 2021, sentenced to life without parole on 14 October 2021, charged in New York with the murder of Kathleen McCormack Durst (October-November 2021) and died in custody on 10 January 2022, so that case never went to trial. Durst is drawn only as an anonymous rim-lit silhouette (not a likeness, never a photo or interview recreation), never posed heroically; the only words of his are the reported bathroom remarks, on a 'wording as reported' card that also says the audio was later shown to be re-ordered in editing. The victims are named only on the memorial card and are never shown; no violence, weapon, body, home or crime scene is drawn; the 2001 Texas case is omitted entirely. The note, envelope and letter are generic drawings (tagged 'not the real note' / 'not the real letters'), showing only the reported word 'CADAVER' and the reported 'BEVERLEY' misspelling, with no address. The studio, corridor, bathroom door and hotel corridor are generic illustrations with no HBO branding, logo, room number or real set; the microphone is a generic lavalier with no brand. Every card is our own typed graphic; no real police, court or HBO material is imitated. No dialogue is invented. Legal status verified 2026-10-13.",
